{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "recipe-zimage-turbo.img2img",
  "revision": 5,
  "title": "Z-Image Turbo: image to image",
  "description": "Prompt-guided image to image with Z-Image Turbo: the source image is encoded to a latent and sampled again at a denoise below 1, so the prompt reshapes the image while lower denoise keeps more of its structure. It is not instruction editing: the model doesn't follow edit instructions, it renders the prompt starting from the source. The source image is the task's source image, a file in ComfyUI's input folder. The output has the source image's size, rounded down to multiples of 8 by the VAE encode, so the task's width and height must be the source's, and the contract check refuses a source whose sides aren't multiples of 8.",
  "kind": "image",
  "operations": [
    "image_edit"
  ],
  "graph": {
